<title>BAHRAIN: United Saudi Commercial Bank nine-month net rises.</title>
<headline>United Saudi Commercial Bank nine-month net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			 (million riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit			257.6	    vs  235.9</p>
<p> Operating income		638.7	    vs  645.6</p>
<p> Operating expenses	    403.8	    vs  421.0</p>
<p> Other income		     22.7	    vs   11.3</p>
<p> Provision			  30.0	    vs   22.5</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity	    1.79 billion vs    1.63 billion</p>
<p> Total assets		     11.73 billion vs   11.59 billion</p>
<p> Total deposits		    5.87 billion vs    5.62 billion</p>
<p>Full Name: United Saudi Commercial Bank</p>
<p>NOTE: Bank Melli Iran and United Bank of Pakistan each hold a 10 percent stake in the Riyadh-based bank. The rest is owned by Saudi Arabian investors.</p>
</text>
